  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Restoring the Environment and Strengthening Resilience of Rohingya Refugees and Host Communities in Cox&#x2019;s Bazar</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will contribute to the resilience of Rohingya refugees and host communities through community led disaster risk reduction (DRR), improvement of the communities&#x2019; resilience and community empowerment. The project will prioritize integrative strategies to contribute to the resilience of the communities living in areas affected by disasters in the area of the Balukhali watershed with a focus on their engagement in disaster prevention, preparedness, response and recovery efforts. Specific activities include community-led risk reduction, including operation and maintenance of the water sanitation and hygiene infrastructure, increased awareness, and promotion of improved resilience and environmental rehabilitation. The integrated watershed management for the Balukhali stream will contribute to immediate DRR ensuring decent living conditions and strengthening of communities&#x2019; resilience during disasters. Longer term impact will also include environmental rehabilitation and a more resilient ecosystem.</narrative>
  </description>
